    [Doc][Model] Align shared GLM-5.2/5.3 deployment settings and W4A4C8 examples (#17516)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Merge GLM-5.2/GLM-5.3 deployment documentation and align shared
    configurations with the maintained release guide. Script source is
    `releases/v0.30.0` at `1bd04a362691d78286399916c03821a201b66a8e`, the
    branch containing the earlier GLM documentation updates, rather than the
    incomplete main guide or frozen rc2 branch. This PR continues to target
    main.
    
    - Import the release A2/A3 colocated, PD, MemCache KV pool and 1M DCP
    scripts. Include the A2 DP-rank and parameter nesting corrections,
    eight-node A2 PD/pooling topology, and RC1 compatibility instructions.
    - Use explicit RC2 image tags and document the release source snapshot.
    Retain the version-pinned W4A4C8 self-test environment separately.
    Synchronize Flash A2 rank/layout corrections from the same release
    branch.
    - Default shared examples to GLM-5.3 while retaining model-specific
    checkpoint choices. Preserve the A5 W4A4C8 single-node, PP2 colocated
    and PD examples; all seven A5 commands use inline checkpoint paths.
    Remove W4A8 examples and weight references from the merged guide.
    - Retain the local 2026-10-10 W4A4C8 validation: GLM-5.2 and GLM-5.3
    passed startup and short HTTP requests. GLM-5.3 GSM8K attempted 1319
    samples, answered 1279 correctly (96.97%), including 10 request errors
    in the denominator. GLM-5.2 has no dataset score from that validation.
    Record the historical parser/image/checkpoint limitations.
    - Unify the merged guide's served model name as `glm`, matching curl
    verification. Correct the PD tuning references and describe SFA
    TurboQuant V1 support in the selected release branch.
    - Keep merged navigation and support-matrix links, plus Flash checkpoint
    metadata and version-pinned historical examples. The previous
    multi-commit history was rebuilt on main before these follow-up updates
    to remove the old CI rebase conflict.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Documentation and navigation only. No runtime changes.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - MkDocs strict build passed.
    - 106 Shell blocks passed `bash -n`; 5 Python blocks passed AST parsing;
    114 embedded JSON objects parsed successfully.
    - All deployment code blocks from the selected GLM-5.3 and Flash release
    guides are retained; the only GLM-5.3 runtime-argument normalization is
    the served model name `glm`.
    - Verified the A2 PD/pool/RC1 compatibility anchors, consistent service
    model names, explicit RC image tags, no W4A8 in the merged guide, and
    inline paths in all A5 tabs.
    - Markdownlint, codespell, typos and `git diff --check` passed. Ruff
    checks passed for the earlier navigation changes.
    - The full formatting script was previously attempted but stalled
    installing actionlint's Go dependency; relevant file checks were run
    individually.
    - No NPU services, accuracy evaluations or performance benchmarks were
    rerun for this synchronization. Historical startup/GSM8K results do not
    establish the current parser change, actual 135K inputs, tool use or a
    throughput gate.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/a98247ab4db686ee03c66d5feb3c761e52a2f8ab
    
